Task: Culling, indirect draws, tile memory and half precision. The level is drawn in 16-unit cells (Blood Gulch: 79 to 245 draws), each culled to the camera, each sun cascade and each light face; objects are culled by sphere per shadow map. CullingTests matches brute force over five views (65% of the opaque draws culled). The frame is unchanged (13.1 to 13.2 ms at 4K): it is bound by the screen passes and by passes at the output size, not by geometry. Hi-Z, PVS and argument buffers are not built; nothing in play can be memoryless; half precision is left to the Phase 17 tiers.
